h perspectives are able to interact  to create one cohesive whole in light of  the recent events and our current  situation one might ask is it still  important that we study our disciplines  to pursue our callings to strive to be  people of character to search for truth  is any of this relevant does it matter  it seems clear to me that it matters now  more than ever although it might be  tempting to  that are approaching this problem from a  single perspective such as science or  prayer in reality it will require the  combination of many perspectives working  together we need scientists and people  from all disciplines who understand the  synergistic way knowledge reason and  faith interact who bring knowledge and  passion for understanding the science  will work collaboratively with people  from many different specialties toward a  common goal and have the strength of  character necessary to make the  decisions that are difficult and often  required one such person comes to mind  dr. Francis Collins who recently did an  interview about Cove in 19 dr. Collins  is a well-known respected scientist who  was the head of the human genome project  one of two scientific research endeavors  that we're working on discovering the  nucleic acid instruction book that is  within our DNA he is currently the  director of the NIH otherwise known as  the National Institute of Health  although the majority of the interview  focused on what we have learned about  the virus and what we should do to  address this pandemic it became apparent  that he was not making any of his  decisions within a vacuum but rather  through many conversations with a number  of experts in various fields throughout  each day dr. Collins who is deciding  which theories projects and clinical  trials to run recognizes the necessity  of these conversations - making the  right decisions but more importantly he  also knows that these decisions need to  occur within a larger framework this  became apparent when dr. Collins  answered the question is there a limit  on how much of the public's money we  should spend on one human life dr.  Collins replied when it comes to the  dollars and the sons you know I am a  Christian I do pay close attention  the way in which Jesus in all his  parables and in all the ways he lived  his life emphasized the value of every  human life and to say okay this just  passed way too much and that next  seventy year old we just got to let him  go I can't go there as a Christian and  probably partly because I'm a physician  I don't think most people would feel all  that comfortable with that trade-off dr.  Collins's answers throughout the  interview Illustrated a knowledge and  passion for his science the need for the  conversations with others of different  expertise to understand the problem and  the importance of that ethical framework  to guide that discovery the expertise of  many of from a variety of different  disciplines and perspectives is what  we're going to need to navigate such  complex issues as we're facing with  today at Hillsdale College our goal is  to equip you for participating in the  conversations required to navigate  through the issues of life and to do  that the journey goes beyond what we  teach you in the classroom it exists in  the time you spend figuring out what you  study why it's your passion and how to  integrate all these ideas within a  larger framework you are in a group of  colleagues who are all searching for  truth from their perspective of they're  very disciplined toes and discipline  each contributing to the conversation  each bringing their expertise and  experiences to the discussion the casual  conversations before and after class in  the hallway over a meal the study  session conversations when you're trying  to understand a difficult concept the  late-night spontaneous conversations and  the dorm are all important to being at  Hillsdale they are what has been missing  since we are no longer together here and  interacting as a community of course we  are still helping you learn and gain  understanding as we complete the  semester in every possible way  including  zooom classrooms it's just not the same  the interchange of ideas as we teach and  challenge each other to grow in  knowledge reason character faith is  necessary ideally this fall we will be  able to be back here together in  community finding our passions gaining  the knowledge to pursue them and having  our conversations for those of you who  will not be returning in the fall our  seniors remember the importance of these  ideas relationships and conversations  that challenge and help you grow while  you were at Hillsdale thank you seniors  for the many times you've included me in  these conversations for I am certain  that they have changed me and allowed me  to grow in knowledge character and faith  remember to the countless hours you  wrestled with the challenging idea or  problem to grow in knowledge and  understanding remember the many  opportunities you had to debate what you  believe and why you believe it use this  knowledge to follow your calling to be a  person of character to discern in each  moment the best way to live as you  graduate from Hillsdale and begin to  pursue the next phase in your life  remember as it says in Joshua 1:9 be  strong and courageous do not be afraid  do not be dismayed for the Lord your God  is with you do not forget to keep  learning having those conversations  searching for truth being grateful and  praying because it matters thank you  please stand for the benediction and now  may the god of peace who brought again  from the dead our Lord Jesus Christ's  the great Shepherd of the Sheep by the  blood of the eternal covenant equip you  for every good work to do his will  working in us that which is well  pleasing in his sight and the blessing  of our Lord Jesus Christ God his father  and the Holy Spirit be with us all and  remain with us evermore  amen  [Music]  [App